-- A non-neighbour connection in a compositional run.  Thirty cells in a row,
-- three components plus water, no wells.  The initial pressure falls from
-- 150 bar in cell 1 to 121 bar in cell 30, so every connection carries a flow.
-- An NNC joins cells 3 and 28, which share no face; the flow across it follows
-- from its transmissibility alone.
--
-- The NNC transmissibility of 1.0 is about twelve times that between
-- neighbours, so cells 3 and 28 reach the same pressure within the first
-- report step.  Without the NNC they are still about 11 bar apart then.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
RUNSPEC
------------------------------------------------------------------------
TITLE
   A NON-NEIGHBOUR CONNECTION ACROSS A COMPOSITIONAL ROW

METRIC

TABDIMS
/
OIL
GAS
WATER
DIMENS
30 1 1
/

COMPS
3 /

FULLIMP

START
  1 'JAN' 2016  /

REGDIMS
1 1 0 0 /

UNIFIN
UNIFOUT

